This repository contains a portable public evaluation pipeline adapted from
Goedel-Prover-V2:

https://github.com/Goedel-LM/Goedel-Prover-V2

The technical Python pipeline, shell orchestration, environment files,
toolchain files, and configuration files adapt public upstream material and
conventions for prompt construction, proof extraction, Lean verification, and
benchmark-specific evaluation. The upstream README identifies
Goedel-Prover-V2 as licensed under the Apache License 2.0. This distribution
retains the Apache License 2.0 text in LICENSE.

DeepSeek-Prover-V2-7B model configuration targets the public model checkpoint:

https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-Prover-V2-7B

This repository records the reviewed model revision in configuration metadata.
Users supply the model path at run time. This distribution does not include
model weights or tokenizer snapshots.

Gitlinks, Lake declarations, and Lake manifest pins identify Lean, Mathlib,
and REPL sources:

https://github.com/leanprover/lean4
https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4
https://github.com/leanprover-community/repl

Benchmark data comes from upstream benchmark projects. Users must obtain the
data from those projects and comply with their licenses:

https://github.com/openai/miniF2F
https://github.com/zhangir-azerbayev/ProofNet
https://github.com/leanprover-community/PutnamBench
https://github.com/frenzymath/FATE
